# Implementation Plan - AES-256 Encrypted Database Credentials & Centralized Security Module

Secure all database credentials (`DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_NAME`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASSWORD`) using AES-256 symmetric encryption (Fernet). Replace plain-text `.env` credentials with encrypted ciphertext, separate the Master Secret Key from source control, centralize credential access in `app/database/config.py`, and enforce TLS/SSL wire encryption on MySQL database connections.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Zero Plain-Text Credentials**: Plain-text credentials will be removed from `.env` and replaced with an encrypted payload string `ENCRYPTED_DB_CONFIG`.
> - **Master Secret Key Separation**: The Master Secret Key will be stored in `.master.key` at the workspace root, which will be added to `.gitignore`. Alternatively, `MASTER_SECRET_KEY` can be set in OS environment variables.
> - **Database Functionality & Safety**: Database tables, schemas, and data will remain completely untouched. The backend modules will connect seamlessly using the in-memory decrypted credentials.

